# oracle-inputs: w229xf_efield_tip4p.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 4.7e-14, atoms 4.5e-12. (atoms above 1e-12: TIP4P M-site arithmetic order; still far inside the 1e-8 tolerance)
# oracle: 27 rigid-free TIP4P/2005 waters (lj/cut/tip4p/cut, no kspace; cutoff 4.5 A keeps every Coulomb pair below half the box) in a uniform field with fix efield/tip4p (constant field, energy on via fix_modify); flexible bonds, nve
units           real
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
read_data       w229xf_efield_tip4p.data
pair_style      lj/cut/tip4p/cut 1 2 1 1 0.1546 4.5
pair_coeff      1 1 0.1852 3.1589
pair_coeff      1 2 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 0.0 1.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 450.0 0.9572
angle_style     harmonic
angle_coeff     1 55.0 104.52
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.5
fix             1 all nve
fix             3 all efield/tip4p 0.3 -0.2 0.5
fix_modify      3 energy yes
thermo_style    custom step temp pe press f_3
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             50
